{"record": {"artifacts": [{"id": "arxiv:2505.13032", "kind": "paper", "locator": "linked URL", "url": "https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.13032"}, {"id": "gh:ddlBoJack/MMAR", "kind": "repo", "locator": "GitHub repository URL", "url": "https://github.com/ddlBoJack/MMAR"}, {"id": "hf:BoJack/MMAR", "kind": "dataset", "locator": "Hugging Face dataset URL", "url": "https://huggingface.co/datasets/BoJack/MMAR"}], "categories": ["强推理", "Strong Reasoning", "多模态", "Multimodal", "推理", "Reasoning", "MMAR", "音频语言模型", "深度推理", "多模态模型", "VLM", "逻辑推理", "音频理解", "Audio Understanding", "不支持", "Unsupported"], "description": {"en": "We introduce MMAR, a new benchmark comprising 1,000 meticulously curated audio-question-answer triplets, designed to evaluate the deep reasoning capabilities of Audio-Language Models (ALMs) across massive multi-disciplinary tasks.", "zh": "MMAR是一个全新评测基准，旨在评估音频-语言模型（ALMs）的深度推理能力。该基准包含1,000个精心构建的音频与问答，并经过多轮纠错与质量校验以确保高标准。与现有局限于特定声音、音乐或语音领域的评测体系不同，MMAR覆盖现实场景中的混合模态，并采用四级分层分类体系（信号层、感知层、语义层与文化层）。该基准中的每个题目都需要超越表层理解的多层次深度推理，部分问题更要求研究生级别的专业领域知识与感知能力。我们在MMAR上评估了多类模型，测试结果表明该基准具有显著挑战性，分析结果进一步揭示了当前模型在理解与推理能力上的关键局限。我们期待MMAR能推动这个重要但尚未充分探索的研究领域的发展。"}, "documents": [{"document_type": "registry_page", "id": "opencompass_hub:https://hub.opencompass.org.cn/dataset-detail/MMAR", "source": "opencompass_hub", "source_url": "https://hub.opencompass.org.cn/dataset-detail/MMAR", "title": "MMAR"}], "evidence_summary": {"document_count": 1, "model_count": null, "model_count_basis": null}, "key": "opencompass:1910", "languages": [], "modality": "multimodal", "name": "MMAR", "openness": {"access_gate": "none", "basis": "Row 2: code_public=yes; data_located=found; data_license=non-commercial/no-derivs/custom_or_other", "code_license": null, "code_license_note": null, "data_license": "CC-BY-NC-4.0", "data_license_note": null, "data_located": "found", "evidence": [{"evidence_url": "https://huggingface.co/api/datasets/BoJack/MMAR/tree/main?recursive=true&expand=false", "locator": "file listing: MMAR-